From: OpenWrt RTL8197F bringup <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: 8250_dw: drain RTL8197F RX FIFO earlier

The RTL8197F quirk fixes the UART type to a 16-byte 16550A. Its default
eight-byte RX trigger leaves only eight bytes of headroom during a paste.
Use the one-byte trigger on this UART, leaving fifteen bytes of headroom
while the CPU services the interrupt. Preserve the TX and unrelated FIFO
settings and apply the choice on every termios update, including shell
line-editor transitions. Other DesignWare UARTs keep their existing setup.

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c
@@ -422,6 +422,16 @@ static void dw8250_set_termios(struct uart_port *p, struct ktermios *termios,
 	}
 	clk_prepare_enable(d->clk);
 
+	if (d->pdata && (d->pdata->quirks & DW_UART_QUIRK_RTL8197F)) {
+		struct uart_8250_port *up = up_to_u8250p(p);
+
+		/* Leave room for paste bursts while the interrupt is pending.
+		 * serial8250_do_set_termios() writes this cached FCR to hardware.
+		 */
+		up->fcr &= ~UART_FCR_TRIGGER_MASK;
+		up->fcr |= UART_FCR_ENABLE_FIFO | UART_FCR_R_TRIG_00;
+	}
+
 	dw8250_do_set_termios(p, termios, old);
 }
 
